Open Source First: from buzzword to roadmap 🔌
Everyone is talking about digital sovereignty. Fewer people can explain what it means in practice: what to migrate, what to build, what to buy, and who's actually in control once the contract is signed. DINAconCH 2026, the conference for digital sustainability, wants to answer exactly that.
Guild42.ch is happy to promote our partner event. Here are some of the sessions on the programme:
// "How the Smartphone Duopoly Undermines Digital Sovereignty"
// "Furniture, Not Lumber: What Sausages, Furniture and Airplanes Have to Do with Digital Sovereignty"
// "Der AI-Hebel: Warum der grösste Stromfresser unser bestes Green-IT-Tool ist"
// "Fünf Jahre e-ID und Vertrauensinfrastruktur"
// "Software für alle – aber designed für wen?"
Other sessions look at how digital sovereignty gives us more control over our ecological footprint, and how AI and digital innovation are reshaping mobility. There's plenty more on the programme ⚙️
If you build, operate or buy software in Switzerland, this is a good day to step back and look at where the dependencies in your stack really are.
// NOTE: DINAconCH is a partner event, not organised by Guild42.ch
Date: Wednesday, 18 November 2026
Location: Kongresszentrum Kreuz, Bern
